        "raw": "I may or may not have ever heard this editor's note before today!  No Justifier comment, so no is likely, but maybe he just had nothing to say at the time.\n\nThe show notes could have been vastly improved with pictures, either of skinks (and Christopher's tiny friend if that wasn't one of them), or of the presence or absence of Adam's fireplace.  (This is a comment Justifier likely wouldn't have thought worth his time.  Turns out Just-A-Fire is a pretty different guy.)\n\nHey, I like Nineties Spiderman.  Okay, I didn't see a lot of it, I was more of an X-Men kid, but still, what there was was better than more recent \"improvements\" imo.\n\nAi ai ai, rules lawyers...always having to have THE answer, instead of simply grabbing AN answer and calling it good enough.  Christopher flailing for a sufficiently specific wording to avoid any ambiguity saddens me.  Just be inconsistent!  It's fine!\n\nI do feel as if I remember hearing and being angry about that Darken the Sky ruling before....\n\nRadioActivist!(R) The Other Yellowish-Orange Meat!",
